.\" sact.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX sact(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/SACT.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/SACT.
.TH SACT 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
sact \- display SCCS file editing activity
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sact
is not provided on maux.
version control on this project is host-side (git); maux ships
no SCCS implementation at all.
